13 years after a valley teenager was  robbed and killed his mother says today  justice was finally served devon  phillips was the last of four men  involved in the death of eric braille to  be sentenced and now brill's mother is  not holding back  a really disgusting process to me a  13-year fight karen brill says is  finally over devon phillips sentenced to  nine years in prison for the death of  eric brill in 2009 they stole my life  from me they stole everybody  killed him  phillips along with nadine hicko devonte  wash and arthur moore are now all behind  bars for robbery and murder the four men  robbed and opened fire at brill and his  friends outside a house party in 2009  near sloan lane and charleston as they  all ran away brill was shot in the head  while another victim was shot four times  but survived before the sentence  phillips offered these words i know that  sorry will never be enough to bring back  the child's loss i would never be able  to estimate the pain you have to live  with as a mother after the incident  police hit a wall in the investigation  for seven years but eventually found  phillips was sentenced to nine years for  voluntary manslaughter with a deadly  weapon and has two prior convictions for  robbery today with all four men finally  in jail brill's mother says there is  finally some closure i consider myself  fortunate to have had somebody  held accountable even though i'm not  happy with the sentences  that they've received  eric i guess you know he got justice  brill's mother also tells us she will  continue to fight and push to keep these  four men behind bars she says she will  push for stiffer laws and lobby on her  son's behalf
 

